[packages/eslint-plugin-react-hooks/src/index.ts] I might suggest using a `get` accessor here, rather than assigning to an empty object and then re-assigning later.   This is what we're doing in several of the plugins I work on:

e.g. 
https://github.com/eslint-community/eslint-plugin-eslint-plugin/blob/main/lib/index.ts#L71-L75

```ts
recommended: {
  plugins: {
    get 'react-hooks'(): ESLint.Plugin {
      return plugin;
    }
  },
  rules: recommendedRuleConfigs,
},
```

Not a huge difference in the end, but keeps it self-contained.

